<style>
/* ---- page-specific: sample store listing ------------------------------- */
html{scroll-padding-top:74px;}
.demo-note{
  background:rgba(224,192,90,.08);border:1px solid rgba(224,192,90,.45);
  border-left:3px solid var(--amber);border-radius:var(--radius);
  padding:16px 20px;margin:26px 0 0;
}
.demo-note b{color:var(--amber);}
.demo-note p{margin:6px 0 0;color:var(--text-dim);font-size:14px;max-width:820px;}
.listing{display:grid;grid-template-columns:300px 1fr;gap:34px;margin-top:34px;align-items:start;}
@media(max-width:760px){.listing{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px;}}
.cover{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;background:#0b0d11;}
.cover svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;}
.sys-chip{
  display:inline-block;font-family:"Press Start 2P",ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:10px;
  letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--g7000);border:1px solid rgba(59,169,122,.5);
  border-radius:999px;padding:6px 10px;margin-bottom:14px;
}
.listing h1{font-size:clamp(26px,4vw,38px);margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;}
.byline{color:var(--text-dim);font-size:15px;margin:0 0 18px;}
.byline b{color:var(--text);}
.blurb{color:var(--text-dim);font-size:15.5px;max-width:640px;}
.pricerow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:26px 0 8px;}
.price{font-family:"Press Start 2P",ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:24px;color:var(--text);}
.vat{color:var(--text-mute);font-size:12.5px;}
.buy{
  display:inline-block;background:var(--g7000);border:1px solid var(--g7000);color:#07120d;
  font-weight:700;font-size:15px;padding:13px 26px;border-radius:9px;text-decoration:none;
}
.buy:hover{background:#49c48f;text-decoration:none;}
.haskey{
  display:inline-block;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text-dim);
  font-size:14px;padding:12px 20px;border-radius:9px;text-decoration:none;
}
.haskey:hover{border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--text);text-decoration:none;}
.metatable{margin-top:28px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);}
.metatable div{display:flex;gap:16px;padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);font-size:14px;}
.metatable dt{color:var(--text-mute);width:150px;flex-shrink:0;}
.metatable dd{margin:0;color:var(--text-dim);}
.metatable dd b{color:var(--text);}
.flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(215px,1fr));gap:14px;margin-top:26px;}
.flow .step .num{background:var(--g7000);color:#07120d;}
.fine{color:var(--text-mute);font-size:13px;margin-top:18px;max-width:820px;}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<header class="topbar">
  <a class="brand" href="index.html"><span class="brand-mark"><img src="assets/kcmunch.png" alt="" width="22" height="22"></span> Retro Vault</a>
  <nav class="nav">
    <a href="index.html">The Vault</a>
    <a href="sell-your-homebrew.html">For homebrew makers</a>
    <a class="cta-ghost" href="https://demo.retrovault.world" target="_blank" rel="noopener">🕹 Live demo</a>
    <a class="cta" href="index.html#download">Download</a>
  </nav>
</header>

<main id="top">
<div class="wrap">

  <div class="demo-note">
    <b>Sample listing.</b>
    <p><i>Cosmic Courier</i> is not a real game — it is a placeholder we wrote ourselves, so that this
    page can show exactly how a homebrew title is presented and delivered on Retro Vault without
    putting a real author's work on sale before their agreement is signed. Everything around it — the
    price, the checkout, the licence key, the delivery steps — is the real mechanism.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="listing">

    <div class="cover">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 300 400" role="img" aria-label="Box art for the sample game Cosmic Courier">
        <defs>
          <linearGradient id="sky" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#151a2e"/><stop offset="100%" stop-color="#0b0d11"/>
          </linearGradient>
        </defs>
        <rect width="300" height="400" fill="url(#sky)"/>
        <!-- stars -->
        <g fill="#e9edf2">
          <rect x="24" y="52" width="3" height="3"/><rect x="72" y="96" width="2" height="2"/>
          <rect x="128" y="44" width="3" height="3"/><rect x="196" y="78" width="2" height="2"/>
          <rect x="248" y="40" width="3" height="3"/><rect x="264" y="128" width="2" height="2"/>
          <rect x="44" y="150" width="2" height="2"/><rect x="216" y="168" width="3" height="3"/>
          <rect x="96" y="196" width="2" height="2"/><rect x="156" y="132" width="2" height="2"/>
        </g>
        <!-- planet -->
        <circle cx="232" cy="236" r="52" fill="#3ba97a" opacity=".22"/>
        <circle cx="232" cy="236" r="52" fill="none" stroke="#3ba97a" stroke-width="3" opacity=".7"/>
        <rect x="180" y="228" width="104" height="4" fill="#3ba97a" opacity=".5"/>
        <!-- courier ship, blocky on purpose -->
        <g fill="#5b8def">
          <rect x="72" y="236" width="56" height="16"/>
          <rect x="88" y="220" width="28" height="16"/>
          <rect x="60" y="244" width="12" height="8"/>
          <rect x="128" y="240" width="14" height="8"/>
        </g>
        <g fill="#c07de0"><rect x="96" y="224" width="8" height="8"/></g>
        <g fill="#e0c05a"><rect x="48" y="246" width="10" height="4"/><rect x="36" y="247" width="8" height="2"/></g>
        <!-- crate being carried -->
        <g fill="#b98a5f"><rect x="92" y="252" width="20" height="16"/></g>
        <g fill="#0b0d11"><rect x="99" y="252" width="6" height="16"/></g>
        <!-- title plate -->
        <rect x="0" y="312" width="300" height="88" fill="#0f1115"/>
        <rect x="0" y="310" width="300" height="2" fill="#3ba97a"/>
        <text x="150" y="344" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9edf2"
              font-family="'Press Start 2P',monospace" font-size="17">COSMIC</text>
        <text x="150" y="372" text-anchor="middle" fill="#3ba97a"
              font-family="'Press Start 2P',monospace" font-size="17">COURIER</text>
        <text x="150" y="391" text-anchor="middle" fill="#6b7280"
              font-family="'Press Start 2P',monospace" font-size="7">VIDEOPAC G7000</text>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div>
      <span class="sys-chip">● PHILIPS VIDEOPAC G7000 / ODYSSEY²</span>
      <h1>Cosmic Courier</h1>
      <p class="byline">by <b>A. Placeholder</b> · 2026 · Homebrew · 1 player</p>

      <div class="prose blurb">
        <p>Haul cargo between three colonies while the gravity wells shift under you. One button, one
        ship, and a delivery schedule that stops being reasonable somewhere around wave six.</p>
        <p>Written for original hardware and playable in your browser. Buying it gets you the game
        file itself, not a stream: you can keep it, run it in the Vault offline, or load it on a real
        Videopac with a cartridge of your own.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pricerow">
        <span class="price">€4.99</span>
        <!-- LEMON SQUEEZY CHECKOUT LINK GOES HERE (Products -> the product -> Share -> Checkout Link) -->
        <a class="buy" id="buyBtn" href="https://retrovault.lemonsqueezy.com/">Buy — €4.99</a>
        <a class="haskey" href="#delivery">I already have a licence key</a>
      </div>
      <p class="vat">One-time purchase. No subscription. VAT included where applicable — Lemon Squeezy
      is the merchant of record and handles the tax.</p>

      <dl class="metatable">
        <div><dt>What you receive</dt><dd><b>A licence key by email</b>, instant play in the browser, and a downloadable copy of the game file</dd></div>
        <div><dt>File format</dt><dd>.bin cartridge image (2 KB–16 KB, depending on the title)</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Devices</dt><dd>Up to 10 of your own browsers and machines; you can free a slot yourself</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Licence length</dt><dd>Unlimited — the key does not expire</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Refunds</dt><dd>Within 14 days, by replying to your receipt</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Author's share</dt><dd>The revenue goes to the game's author; Retro Vault keeps a small share to cover costs</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section id="delivery">
    <span class="kicker">Delivery</span>
    <h2 class="sec-head">What happens after you press Buy.</h2>
    <p class="sec-sub">No account, no launcher, no waiting for a human. The whole thing takes under a
    minute.</p>

    <div class="flow steps">
      <div class="step">
        <span class="num">1</span>
        <h3>Checkout</h3>
        <p>Payment, VAT and the receipt are handled by Lemon Squeezy as merchant of record. Card,
        iDEAL, PayPal and the other methods they support.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="num">2</span>
        <h3>Licence key by email</h3>
        <p>Lemon Squeezy issues a unique key for the order and emails it straight away. Nothing to
        register, no password to pick.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="num">3</span>
        <h3>Paste it in the Vault</h3>
        <p>On the game's page, <b>I have a licence key</b> → paste → the game unlocks in that browser
        and starts. The key works on up to ten of your own machines.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="num">4</span>
        <h3>Keep your copy</h3>
        <p>Download the game file and keep it — it runs in the offline Vault or any emulator. Each
        copy carries an invisible code tied to the order.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="fine">Retro Vault is a free, offline game library for the Philips Videopac G7000/G7400,
    Magnavox Odyssey², Commodore 64, Commodore Amiga and MS-DOS: box art, manuals, history and
    gameplay clips for around 400 releases, with the emulators built in. Out-of-print titles play
    straight away; for anything still commercially sold, you bring your own file. This shop exists
    for one narrow purpose: so that people still writing <i>new</i> games for these machines have a
    place to sell them, with the revenue going to them.</p>
  </section>

</div><!-- /wrap -->
</main>

<footer>
  <div class="f-brand"><img src="assets/kcmunch.png" alt="" width="18" height="18"> RETRO VAULT</div>
  <p>© Don Miguel · Retro Vault License v1.0 · <a href="https://github.com/donmiguel-stack/retrovault">GitHub</a></p>
